{"name":"Tangled Vines","hex":"#cac19a","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tangled","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Mixed up, interlaced.","Intricate."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of tangle"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tangled"},{"term":"vines","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of vine"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vines"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tangled","blocks":[{"text":"Tangled is a 2010 American animated musical fantasy comedy film directed by Nathan Greno and Byron Howard, written by Dan Fogelman, and loosely based on the German fairy tale \"Rapunzel\". Produced by Walt Disney Animation Studios, it stars Mandy Moore, Zachary Levi, and Donna Murphy. The film tells the story of Rapunzel (Moore), a young princess with magical long blonde hair who tries to leave her secret tower. She accepts the aid of an intruder, the outlaw Flynn Rider (Levi), to take her out into the world which she has never seen."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/a8/Tangled_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tangled","wikidata":"Q188439"},{"title":"Vine","blocks":[{"text":"A vine is any plant with a growth habit of trailing or scandent stems, lianas, or runners. The word vine can also refer to such stems or runners themselves, for instance, when used in wicker work."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/%22A_Momordica_charantia-_bitter_guard_plant%22.jpg/330px-%22A_Momordica_charantia-_bitter_guard_plant%22.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vine","wikidata":"Q917284"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Fragonard%2C_The_Swing.jpg/500px-Fragonard%2C_The_Swing.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campa